  "handoff": {
    "summary": "Added a machine-readable dense matrix audit with quick, routine, and full modes; audited 14 public surfaces per domain; verified all 14 over ZZ, QQ, GF(2), and GF(7); recorded row/column swaps over GF(2^61-1) as capability holes; separated process/bootstrap/order-dependent-first/warm timings; classified only routes emitted inside timed invocation windows; and compared identical deterministic workloads with SageMath.",
    "risks": [
      "Cross-host timings are intentionally reported rather than ratcheted; retain reports on Linux x64, Linux arm64, and Darwin arm64.",
      "GF(2^61-1) row/column swaps are public capability holes and most large-word-prime operations emit no backend trace.",
      "The lane needed a local M4RI build because the shared parallel cache did not provision that package.",
      "This benchmark-only change has Linux x64 receipts. Cross-host Linux arm64 and Darwin arm64 reports are follow-up performance evidence, not merge gates or portability claims."
    ],
    "next_steps": [
      "Implement canonical arbitrary-word-prime storage with bulk range ingress, direct swaps, and traceable algorithms.",
      "Replace selection-and-reconstruction swaps with direct exact/resource and packed operations.",
      "Profile and batch GF(2) random fill with common pre-generated random bits.",
      "Retain comparable JSON reports from Linux arm64 and Darwin arm64 before selecting architecture-specific crossovers."
    ]
  }
